hi my name's samuel leeds i'm a property  investor and developer and i've been  investing in property now for 12 years  i've done over 300 property deals  and i'm going to share in this video my  knowledge with you into how  you can predict what the end value is  going to be on a property  because if you're doing a property let's  say it's a fix and flip or  let's say you're buying it to add value  and then to refinance it we call those  brr by refurbished refinance rent or  burr deals how do you this is the golden  question  to property developers and property  investors how do you predict  what the end value is going to be  because if you buy a property  let's say for a hundred thousand pounds  and you fix it up  and you think once this is done it's  going to be worth 200 000 pounds  but then it gets down valued by a valuer  or if you're trying to sell it  no one wants to buy it for two hundred  thousand pounds that's a problem  because it was only worth two hundred  thousand pounds in your mind  in your optimistic rose-colored glasses  mind and the problem with a lot of  entrepreneurs is they do tend to be  optimistic so  how do you be realistic rather than  optimistic when it comes to the end  value  so there's three things that you can do  the first thing you can do  is when you're first looking at the  property let's say it's an auction  property  and you and you're looking at it and  you're trying to think okay what's the  end value i would approach  three independent estate agents  and say to them i've got this property  it's on church road  this is the property what do you think  the value would be if it was done up  nice  what would be the end value and they'll  give you an idea now the problem with a  lot of  uh property developers is they'll speak  to the estate agent that's actually  selling the house  now the estate that's selling the house  they'll tell you what you want to hear  because they just want to sell you the  house so first thing speak to three  independent estate agents and get their  advice because they know they're gonna  have more a better idea than just about  anybody because that's what they do day  in day out  they sell houses i used to be an estate  agent i used to work in great bar  birmingham  and i knew the great bar area really  really well so that's the first thing  speak to three independent estate agents  not  the one estate agent that's selling you  the house by the way if you're enjoying  this video do me a massive favor  smash the like button okay smash the  like button second way  is to do your own due diligence and you  can do this by let's say you've got a  property  again on church road you go on  rightmove.co.uk  and there's other websites you can do  this you can go on mouseprice.com  there are other websites but what you  want to do is you want to look up  these sold houses in that street  over the last two years and try and  stick within quarter of a mile  now if there are no sold properties in  that street or within quarter of a mile  you can look up to half a mile but the  further you go  away from the house the less like for  like it is  and you want to see what property has  sold  that's similar to this property within  quarter of a mile  over the last two years and again if  there's nothing that sold over the last  two years maybe look over the last three  or four years  but again if you start looking at what  happened five six seven eight years ago  that was a completely different market  then and house prices do  change they do fluctuate now by finding  by finding like for like comparables  yourself again really important don't be  optimistic  don't say well this property sold for  100 grand in the street therefore mine  well  because maybe that property was had an  extension  so you need to be finding a like for  like so that's the second thing  do your own due diligence find like for  like properties that sold  within the last two years within quarter  of a mile  and then the third thing you can do is  if you really need to know exactly what  the end value is going to be  is you can just pay a few hundred pounds  to have a valuer go out to the property  and tell you what the end value is going  to be now  they'll they're going to tell you based  on the quality of the refurb so they  might say if the refurb's to a really  high standard  the n value is going to be 200 000  pounds and it's important to get an idea  of what kind of  quality the refurb needs to be done but  that's the third way  if it's a big project and it's you know  it's potentially  a unique property and you're putting a  lot of money and a lot of risk into the  deal  always get a valuer to go out and tell  you what they predict the end value to  be  another little tip is if you want to be  conservative knock off 10  of what you think the end value will be  of what you think the value's going to  knock off 10  because you do not want to be overly  optimistic and then get caught out  when the when the property gets down  valued so those are the three ways i  hope you found this video useful  get three independent estate agents do  your own due diligence and look at local  properties that have sold in the area  and if all else fails  get a valuer to go to the property there  are other things you can do as well  and we do go into great detail at the  property investors crash course  about how to value a house how to  negotiate the house and we go through  the whole process so  if you've not been to the property  investors crash course i'd like to give  you a free gift  you can come on the house is two days  with me i'll leave a link in the  description  and again subscribe to the channel and i  hope this has been helpful i'll see you  next time thanks
 

